  "$comment": "U-157. The RPG gunner: a rifleman's body with a launcher, tuned by its archetype's `launcher` block (enemies.json). With a threat known: inside the near edge of its band, or with no rockets left, the rifle is in its hands and it fights as a rifleman does from cover (relocate when flanked; in cover, reload when low, peek and fire a burst unless pressured, else stay down; else take cover; with none, fight in the open). Otherwise the launcher is in its hands: first, moving to other cover in its band after a shot; then a rocket at a target it knows has stood still, in its band, behind cover or with others about it, searched clear of every friend and itself, after a wind-up on a locked point; else new cover in its band when flanked, stay down in cover (reloading), or take cover in its band (never inside its near edge); with none, its rifle in the open. It takes no group role and throws no grenade. Nothing known: at ease, launcher in hand. U-010: first of all, a lever job the session gave it, as the MG's tree.",
